# Frozen-content manifest — Impilo vNext Hybrid / Federated Target Architecture
#
# Recorded at architecture freeze, 2026-08-05, under ADR-0054.
#
# The digest below pins the EXACT bytes of the frozen baseline. The governance verifier
# recomputes it on every run and fails on any difference. That is the point: a frozen
# document that can be edited without anyone noticing is not frozen, it is merely
# labelled frozen — and this repository has already produced eight controls that held
# only because nothing contradicted them.
#
# HOW TO CHANGE THE FROZEN DOCUMENT
#
#   Substantive change  — any change to doctrine, technical design, operating model,
#                         schemas, contracts, gates, journey behaviour or acceptance
#                         meaning. NOT permitted here. Cut a new version (v1.3.9, v1.4,
#                         or a later successor), archive v1.3.8 with a banner, and move
#                         the pointer. The new version gets its own digest line.
#
#   Governed erratum    — a correction that changes none of the above (a superseded
#                         cross-reference, a stale range, a typo). Permitted. Mark the
#                         change at its site as an erratum with its date, update the
#                         digest below in the SAME commit, and state in the commit
#                         message what was corrected and why it is non-substantive.
#
# Updating this digest without one of those two justifications defeats the mechanism.
# The digest is a tripwire, not a lock: it cannot stop an edit, it can only ensure the
# edit is deliberate and declared.
#
